# Build context of the server and client images (context: the repository root).
# A WHITELIST, like .gitignore: everything is left out, then only what
# server/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile copy is let back in. An image built
# from a working copy thus gets the same inputs as one built from a clean
# clone, without local documentation, tools, data, tests or release drops.
# apple-edge/ is built from its own context (./apple-edge, own .dockerignore).
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!shared/
!server/
!client/

# Never in a build context, even inside the folders above (same rules as
# .gitignore)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/docs
**/*.md
**/*.bat
**/*.cmd
**/*.ps1
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/Thumbs.db
# Hidden files and folders: .env files, caches, secrets, editor and
# workstation tool folders. A hidden file the build needs takes a "!"
# exception placed after this line.
**/.*

# Tests and test data stay local: never compiled into an image
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
**/*e2e*
**/__tests__
**/testdata
**/test-resolve.mjs

# Données locales du poste : jamais versionnées ni dans un build
.cache
